WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.550
Between 1970 and 1995, Asia's cereal
production rose from 313 to 650 million tonnes

2
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.710
a year.

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.750
Alongside it: new
high-yielding wheat and rice,

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.370
spreading across Asia from the late 1960s.

5
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:21.050
By 1980, they grew on about 40
per cent of Asia's cereal area.

6
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.650
By 2000, about 80.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.550
But why did they race through some
places and crawl through others?

8
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.810
Did some farmers just refuse new ideas?

9
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.290
In this mission, you'll learn how
innovations and diseases diffuse:

10
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.690
contagious, hierarchical and relocation.

11
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:43.770
Then you'll plot adoption as an S-curve,
and map diffusion like a geographer.

12
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.690
Your mission: explain why the new seeds
spread fast in some places and slowly

13
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:49.710
in others.
